# Implementation Plan: Real-Time F1 Telemetry Dashboard

Design and implement a real-time telemetry dashboard to visualize live multi-driver Formula 1 metrics (speed, RPM, gear, throttle, brake, track position X/Y) ingested into BigQuery and Pub/Sub.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dashboard Technology Options**:
> 1. **Option A (Recommended - High-Performance Web App)**: **FastAPI + WebSockets + Modern Vanilla Frontend (HTML5 Canvas + Chart.js)**.
>    - True real-time sub-second streaming via WebSockets.
>    - Live 2D Track Map visualizing car coordinates (`x_pos`, `y_pos`) moving across the circuit.
>    - F1 Dark Cockpit aesthetics: Live speedometers, RPM gauge, throttle/brake pedal bars, gear indicators, and driver selector.
> 2. **Option B (Python-Only)**: **Streamlit**.
>    - Built entirely in Python using `streamlit`. Auto-refreshes periodically (1–2s interval).
>    - Simpler to maintain in pure Python, but less fluid for real-time 60fps track animations.

> [!NOTE]
> **Data Feed Strategy for Real-Time Visuals**:
> - The dashboard can query **BigQuery** (`f1_insights.telemetry_realtime`) for latest windowed data or recent batch aggregates, AND/OR subscribe directly to **Pub/Sub** or a lightweight broadcast socket from the pipeline to stream events with minimal latency.

